+    `runtime_launch_unauthorized` with reason `deadline_unavailable` and no
+    `execve`. That branch is **not reachable through an input**: gate 1 has
+    already established that descriptor 3 is a FIFO, and a FIFO is pollable, so
+    the only way to observe the branch is fault injection at the seam. It is
+    specified and tested anyway because the alternative to refusing is waiting
+    forever, and "this cannot fail" is exactly the assumption revision 4 made
+    about the arming call and got wrong. State the injection in the test's own
+    evidence, so no reader mistakes it for an input-driven case.
